KZ2 patch 6079: resident raw vertex streams for the GPU vertex fetch, the pure part (LD_VTX_RES;
design F step 1 of the RE notes earlier change, sub-step b1). Adds libs/video/rsx_vtx_res.h only; nothing includes it
yet, so the build and every run are unchanged.

Patch 2076 (LD_VTX_GPU) decodes the raw big-endian guest bytes in the vertex shader but copies every draw's raw spans
into the upload ring (~11 MB a frame). This header keeps the raw bytes resident instead: a pool of 4 KB
blocks the GPU reads in place, one current block per guest page in use, copied once per write generation of the page;
a draw passes 2076's attribute rows plus, per merged span, the list of its pages' blocks, and the shader reads span byte
a at pool offset (list[a >> 12] << 12) | (a & 4095). The generation comes from patch 6077's OS write watch (shared
state: stamps, arm before the copy, clean while no newer stamp), which reports every writer (PPU stores, SPU puts and
atomics, file reads). A page found clean stands for the walker's epoch (vr_epoch at each wait for the guest);
ASSUMPTION: the guest-sync rule keeps writes out of an epoch for pages a later draw of it reads; LD_VTX_RES=verify
compares every reuse with the checksum of its copy. Blocks are overwritten only after the frames that read them are
complete (last_use per block, frames from 1, 0 = never used; a new generation takes a new block). Allocation prefers a
spare block (never used or retired) from a FIFO in retirement order, and only when none of the first VR_SCAN (4,096)
is safe does a clock hand evict a current page; neither phase looks at more than VR_SCAN entries, and neither takes a
block used in the last two frames or not yet complete. The decode is 2076's RSX_VG_SHARED with the span's list offset passed down
(RSX_VR_SHARED); vr_write_table converts 2076's plan of a draw into the table. Own design; not from upstream.

Tests: tools/runtime/test_vtx_res.sh (decode equal to 2076's bit for bit over 3,000 random draws; 300,000-step
residency stress with a model write watch and a GPU three frames behind: 0 stale pages, 0 in-flight overwrites;
directed cases; negative controls: a blind watch, an ignored fence, writes inside an epoch, a first-fit allocator that evicts a
current page while a retired block is free, each caught; the test refuses a stale patched toolkit).

An earlier change: verify splits bad into bad_stand / bad_clean (which rule kept the page) and, with vr_state.peek, bad_read /
bad_unread (the bytes the draw reads changed, or only other bytes of the page).

An earlier change: two rules for the wiring (6080). vr_stamp: the caller stamps a draw's blocks again when the draw is
recorded, with the fence value of the list that really reads them (submissions between the map and the record raise
it; the map's stamp only protects the blocks while the draw is mapped). vr_acquire / vr_hold_check: a semaphore acquire
passed before its label holds the wanted value holds the stands (every map queries the write watch) until the label
holds it, which then ends the epoch; more than VR_HOLD_MAX (64) pending makes the hold sticky. Host test cases: a
record after 3 flushes (negative control TEST_NEG=4: the map's stamp only) and a producer write after an unmet acquire
(TEST_NEG=5: no hold).

diff --git a/libs/video/rsx_vtx_res.h b/libs/video/rsx_vtx_res.h
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/libs/video/rsx_vtx_res.h
@@ -0,0 +1,362 @@
+/* KZ2 patch 6079: resident raw vertex streams for the GPU vertex fetch (LD_VTX_RES), the pure part.
+ * Design F step 1 (the RE notes earlier change "F"; an earlier change (b)).
+ *
+ * Patch 2076 (LD_VTX_GPU) lets the vertex shader decode the raw big-endian guest bytes, but copies every draw's raw
+ * spans into the upload ring (~11 MB a frame, the walker's flush wait doubled). Here the raw bytes live in a
+ * pool of 4 KB blocks that the GPU reads in place (t22, one ByteAddressBuffer); each guest page in use has one current
+ * block, copied once per write generation of the page, and a draw passes only a small table: 2076's attribute rows
+ * plus, per merged span, the list of pool blocks of its pages (t20). The shader reads byte a of a span (an address
+ * relative to the span's first page) at pool offset (list[a >> 12] << 12) | (a & 4095).
+ *
+ * Write generation. A resident page is current while no write reached it since its bytes were copied: the OS write
+ * watch of patch 6077 (rsx_tex_ww.h; every writer: PPU stores, SPU DMA puts and atomics, HLE code, file reads, since
+ * all are user-mode stores into the one MEM_WRITE_WATCH reservation) gives the answer per page: collect the span, arm
+ * a page before its copy, the page is clean while no stamp newer than its arm covers it. The watch state is shared with
+ * the texture cache (its stamps keep a write for every other user of the page).
+ *
+ * Epoch stand. A collect costs 2-3 us in the game, so a page found clean (or copied) stands for the rest of
+ * the walker's epoch: vr_epoch() is called wherever the walker waits for the guest (a FIFO park, a semaphore acquire,
+ * a put-pointer refill, a flip). A semaphore acquire the walker passes before its label holds the wanted value (it
+ * does not wait unless GCM_SEMA_ACQUIRE=1) is held (vr_acquire): its producer may write after it, inside the new
+ * epoch, so no page stands until every held label is met (vr_hold_check, at each draw), and that ends the epoch.
+ * ASSUMPTION (the guest-sync rule): the bytes a draw reads are final before the
+ * commands holding that draw become visible to the RSX without a further wait, so no write lands inside an epoch on
+ * a page a later draw of the same epoch reads. LD_VTX_RES=verify checks it: every reuse (stand or watch) compares the
+ * page with the checksum taken at its copy and counts a mismatch as bad (and copies it again).
+ *
+ * Fence safety. A block is overwritten only when the frames that referenced it are complete on the GPU: every block
+ * keeps the frame of its last use; a new generation of a page takes a new block (the old one is retired, not
+ * overwritten) and allocation takes only blocks with last_use <= the last completed frame and not used in the last
+ * `min_age` frames. It prefers a spare block (never used, or retired: an old generation), from a FIFO in retirement
+ * order, looking at most VR_SCAN entries; only when none of those is safe does a clock hand evict a current page (at
+ * most VR_SCAN blocks looked at), so a valid page is never evicted while a safe spare block is in the first VR_SCAN.
+ * Frame contract: frames count from 1 (last_use 0 = never used) and completed < frame. The frame given to vr_map_span
+ * protects the blocks while the draw is mapped; the caller stamps them again with vr_stamp when the draw is recorded,
+ * with the fence value of the list that really reads them (submissions between the map and the record raise it).
+ *
+ * Walker thread only: no locking. Host test: tools/runtime/test_vtx_res.sh (decode equal to 2076's bit for bit,
+ * residency under random writes and frames, three negative controls). */
+#pragma once
+#include "rsx_tex_ww.h"
+#include <stdint.h>
+#include <string.h>
+
+#define VR_PAGE_SHIFT 12u
+#define VR_PAGE (1u << VR_PAGE_SHIFT)
+#define VR_NONE 0xFFFFFFFFu
+#define VR_RETIRED 0xFFFFFFFEu
+#define VR_ROW_BYTES 48u                          /* uint4 {base, stride, fmt, lim}, uint4 {pt, 0, 0, 0}, float4 dflt */
+#define VR_TABLE_BYTES (16u * VR_ROW_BYTES)       /* then the spans' block lists (u32 each) */
+#define VR_HOLD_MAX 64u                           /* pending unmet acquires tracked */
+
+typedef struct {
+    uint32_t page;       /* guest page (index from the watch base) this block holds; VR_NONE free, VR_RETIRED old gen */
+    uint32_t last_use;   /* frame of the last draw that referenced the block (0 = never) */
+    uint32_t epoch;      /* walker epoch in which the page was last copied or found clean */
+    ld_ww_arm_t arm;     /* write-watch arm taken before the copy */
+    uint64_t sum;        /* verify: checksum of the copied bytes */
+} vr_block;
+
+/* Copy VR_PAGE bytes from src into pool block `block` (the caller's pool mapping). */
+typedef void (*vr_copy_fn)(void* user, uint32_t block, const uint8_t* src);
+
+typedef struct {
+    ld_ww_state* ww;
+    uint32_t* map;        /* LD_WW_PAGES entries: guest page -> block + 1 (0 = not resident) */
+    vr_block* blocks;
+    uint32_t n_blocks, hand, min_age;
+    uint32_t* spare;      /* n_blocks entries: FIFO of blocks whose page is VR_NONE or VR_RETIRED (exactly those) */
+    uint32_t spare_head, spare_n;
+    uint32_t epoch;       /* starts at 1 */
+    int verify;
+    vr_copy_fn copy;
+    void* user;
+    uint64_t maps, collects, reuse_stand, reuse_clean, copies, evicts, retires, alloc_fail, bad, too_big, ww_fail;
+    /* Verify split: which rule kept the page (bad_stand: the epoch stand, no query; bad_clean: the
+     * write watch answered clean), and, when peek is set (after vr_init), whether the bytes this draw reads differ
+     * from the copy the GPU reads (bad_read: a stale read) or only other bytes of the page changed (bad_unread). */
+    uint64_t bad_stand, bad_clean, bad_read, bad_unread;
+    const uint8_t* (*peek)(void* user, uint32_t block);   /* the copy of block `block` (verify only), or NULL */
+    /* Acquire hold: semaphore acquires the walker passed before their label held the wanted value
+     * (vr_acquire). While any is pending, or after the table overflowed (sticky), no page stands: every map queries
+     * the write watch, so a producer's write after the acquire is seen as on the CPU path, which reads live bytes. */
+    uint32_t hold_n, hold_sticky;
+    uint32_t hold_ea[VR_HOLD_MAX], hold_want[VR_HOLD_MAX];
+    uint64_t holds, hold_releases, hold_overflow, hold_maps;
+} vr_state;
+
+static inline uint64_t vr_sum(const uint8_t* p)
+{
+    uint64_t h = 0xCBF29CE484222325ull;   /* FNV-1a over 64-bit words */
+    for (uint32_t i = 0; i < VR_PAGE; i += 8) { uint64_t w; memcpy(&w, p + i, 8); h = (h ^ w) * 0x100000001B3ull; }
+    return h;
+}
+
+#ifndef VR_SCAN
+#define VR_SCAN 4096u   /* entries looked at per allocation, in each phase */
+#endif
+
+static inline void vr_init(vr_state* s, ld_ww_state* ww, uint32_t* map, vr_block* blocks, uint32_t* spare,
+                           uint32_t n_blocks, vr_copy_fn copy, void* user, int verify)
+{
+    memset(s, 0, sizeof *s);
+    s->ww = ww; s->map = map; s->blocks = blocks; s->n_blocks = n_blocks; s->copy = copy; s->user = user;
+    s->verify = verify; s->epoch = 1; s->min_age = 2;
+    memset(map, 0, sizeof(uint32_t) * LD_WW_PAGES);
+    s->spare = spare; s->spare_head = 0; s->spare_n = n_blocks;
+    for (uint32_t i = 0; i < n_blocks; i++) {
+        memset(&blocks[i], 0, sizeof blocks[i]); blocks[i].page = VR_NONE; spare[i] = i;
+    }
+}
+
+static inline void vr_spare_push(vr_state* s, uint32_t i)
+{
+    s->spare[(s->spare_head + s->spare_n) % s->n_blocks] = i; s->spare_n++;
+}
+
+/* Safe to overwrite: no in-flight frame reads it and it was not used in the last min_age frames. */
+static inline int vr_block_safe(const vr_state* s, const vr_block* b, uint32_t frame, uint32_t completed)
+{
+    return !(b->last_use > completed || (b->last_use && b->last_use + s->min_age > frame));
+}
+
+/* The walker waited for the guest (park, acquire, put refill, flip): stands of the old epoch end. */
+static inline void vr_epoch(vr_state* s) { s->epoch++; }
+
+/* A semaphore acquire at label address `ea` for value `want`; `met` = the label held it when the walker passed. Either
+ * way the epoch ends. Unmet: hold (no stands) until the label holds the value, checked at each draw by vr_hold_check.
+ * More than VR_HOLD_MAX pending: the hold is sticky (no stands for the rest of the run; counted, never unsound). */
+static inline void vr_acquire(vr_state* s, uint32_t ea, uint32_t want, int met)
+{
+    vr_epoch(s);
+    if (met) return;
+    s->holds++;
+    for (uint32_t i = 0; i < s->hold_n; i++)
+        if (s->hold_ea[i] == ea && s->hold_want[i] == want) return;
+    if (s->hold_n == VR_HOLD_MAX) { s->hold_sticky = 1; s->hold_overflow++; return; }
+    s->hold_ea[s->hold_n] = ea; s->hold_want[s->hold_n] = want; s->hold_n++;
+}
+
+/* At each draw before its map: drop the held acquires whose label now holds the value (`read` returns the label's
+ * value). When the last one goes, the epoch ends: pages copied or found clean during the hold were checked before the
+ * producer finished, so they do not stand into the time after it. Returns 1 while the hold is on. */
+static inline int vr_hold_check(vr_state* s, uint32_t (*read)(void* user, uint32_t ea), void* user)
+{
+    if (s->hold_n) {
+        uint32_t k = 0;
+        for (uint32_t i = 0; i < s->hold_n; i++)
+            if (read(user, s->hold_ea[i]) != s->hold_want[i]) {
+                s->hold_ea[k] = s->hold_ea[i]; s->hold_want[k] = s->hold_want[i]; k++;
+            }
+        if (!k && !s->hold_sticky) { vr_epoch(s); s->hold_releases++; }
+        s->hold_n = k;
+    }
+    return s->hold_n || s->hold_sticky;
+}
+
+/* The draw that mapped `blocks` is recorded in the list that will signal `frame`: keep the newer of the two stamps. */
+static inline void vr_stamp(vr_state* s, const uint32_t* blocks, uint32_t n, uint32_t frame)
+{
+    for (uint32_t i = 0; i < n; i++) {
+        vr_block* b = &s->blocks[blocks[i]];
+        if (b->last_use < frame) b->last_use = frame;
+    }
+}
+
+/* A safe block: a spare one first (oldest retirement first), else a current page evicted by the clock hand. */
+static inline uint32_t vr_alloc(vr_state* s, uint32_t frame, uint32_t completed)
+{
+#ifndef VR_ALLOC_FIRST_FIT   /* test-only negative control: the plain first-fit clock over every block */
+    const uint32_t ns = s->spare_n < VR_SCAN ? s->spare_n : VR_SCAN;
+    for (uint32_t k = 0; k < ns; k++) {
+        uint32_t* e = &s->spare[(s->spare_head + k) % s->n_blocks];
+        const uint32_t i = *e;
+        if (!vr_block_safe(s, &s->blocks[i], frame, completed)) continue;
+        *e = s->spare[s->spare_head];   /* take it: the head entry fills its place, the head advances */
+        s->spare_head = (s->spare_head + 1u) % s->n_blocks; s->spare_n--;
+        s->blocks[i].page = VR_NONE;
+        return i;
+    }
+#endif
+    const uint32_t nc = s->n_blocks < VR_SCAN ? s->n_blocks : VR_SCAN;
+    for (uint32_t n = 0; n < nc; n++) {
+        const uint32_t i = s->hand; s->hand = (s->hand + 1u == s->n_blocks) ? 0u : s->hand + 1u;
+        vr_block* b = &s->blocks[i];
+#ifndef VR_ALLOC_FIRST_FIT
+        if (b->page >= VR_RETIRED) continue;   /* spare blocks are taken from the FIFO only */
+#endif
+        if (!vr_block_safe(s, b, frame, completed)) continue;
+        if (b->page < VR_RETIRED) { s->map[b->page] = 0; s->evicts++; }
+        b->page = VR_NONE;
+        return i;
+    }
+    s->alloc_fail++;
+    return VR_NONE;
+}
+
+/* Make the pages of host span [lo, lo + bytes) resident and current for a draw of `frame` (`completed` = the last
+ * frame the GPU finished). out[i] = the block of the span's i-th page. Returns the page count, or -1: too many pages
+ * (> max_pages), the watch failed, or the pool is full; the draw then takes the CPU path (pages already handled stay
+ * consistent). */
+static inline int vr_map_span(vr_state* s, uintptr_t lo, uint32_t bytes, uint32_t frame, uint32_t completed,
+                              uint32_t* out, uint32_t max_pages)
+{
+    ld_ww_state* w = s->ww;
+    s->maps++;
+    if (!ld_ww_in_range(w, lo, bytes)) { s->ww_fail++; return -1; }
+    const uint32_t p0 = (uint32_t)((lo - w->base) >> VR_PAGE_SHIFT);
+    const uint32_t p1 = (uint32_t)((lo - w->base + bytes - 1u) >> VR_PAGE_SHIFT);
+    const uint32_t n = p1 - p0 + 1u;
+    if (n > max_pages) { s->too_big++; return -1; }
+    int need = 0;
+    for (uint32_t p = p0; p <= p1 && !need; p++) {
+        const uint32_t m = s->map[p];
+        need = !m || s->blocks[m - 1u].epoch != s->epoch;
+    }
+    if (!need && (s->hold_n || s->hold_sticky)) { need = 1; s->hold_maps++; }   /* held, no stand */
+    const int stand = !need;   /* every page already current in this epoch: no query */
+    if (need) {
+        s->collects++;
+        if (!ld_ww_collect(w, w->base + ((uintptr_t)p0 << VR_PAGE_SHIFT), n << VR_PAGE_SHIFT)) { s->ww_fail++; return -1; }
+    }
+    for (uint32_t p = p0; p <= p1; p++) {
+        const uintptr_t ph = w->base + ((uintptr_t)p << VR_PAGE_SHIFT);
+        const uint32_t m = s->map[p];
+        vr_block* b = m ? &s->blocks[m - 1u] : NULL;
+        int keep = 0;
+        if (b) {
+            if (stand) { keep = 1; s->reuse_stand++; }
+            else if (ld_ww_clean(w, &b->arm, ph, VR_PAGE)) { keep = 1; s->reuse_clean++; }
+            if (keep && s->verify && vr_sum((const uint8_t*)ph) != b->sum) {
+                s->bad++;
+                if (stand) s->bad_stand++; else s->bad_clean++;
+                if (s->peek) {   /* the span's bytes on this page: [r0, r1) */
+                    const uintptr_t r0 = lo > ph ? lo : ph;
+                    const uintptr_t r1 = lo + bytes < ph + VR_PAGE ? lo + bytes : ph + VR_PAGE;
+                    const uint8_t* cp = s->peek(s->user, (uint32_t)(b - s->blocks));
+                    if (memcmp(cp + (r0 - ph), (const uint8_t*)r0, (size_t)(r1 - r0))) s->bad_read++;
+                    else s->bad_unread++;
+                }
+                keep = 0;
+            }
+            if (!keep) {
+                b->page = VR_RETIRED; s->map[p] = 0; s->retires++;
+#ifndef VR_ALLOC_FIRST_FIT
+                vr_spare_push(s, (uint32_t)(b - s->blocks));
+#endif
+            }
+        }
+        if (keep) {
+            b->epoch = s->epoch;
+        } else {
+            if (stand) {   /* only verify gets here without a collect: collect the page so the arm follows one */
+                s->collects++;
+                if (!ld_ww_collect(w, ph, VR_PAGE)) { s->ww_fail++; return -1; }
+            }
+            const uint32_t i = vr_alloc(s, frame, completed);
+            if (i == VR_NONE) return -1;
+            b = &s->blocks[i];
+            ld_ww_arm(w, &b->arm, ph);   /* after the collect, before the bytes are read */
+            s->copy(s->user, i, (const uint8_t*)ph);
+            if (s->verify) b->sum = vr_sum((const uint8_t*)ph);
+            b->page = p; b->epoch = s->epoch;
+            s->map[p] = i + 1u;
+            s->copies++;
+        }
+        b->last_use = frame;
+        out[p - p0] = (uint32_t)(b - s->blocks);
+    }
+    return (int)n;
+}
+
+/* The decode through the block lists, in the C/HLSL common subset, as 2076's RSX_VG_SHARED with the span's list
+ * offset `pt` (bytes into the draw table) passed down. VR_RAW(pt, a) (the little-endian dword of span byte a,
+ * a % 4 == 0), VG_LUT(i), VG_FN, uint, asint and asfloat come from the including side. */
+#define RSX_VR_SHARED(X) X( \
+VG_FN uint vr_b(uint pt, uint a) { return (VR_RAW(pt, a & 0xFFFFFFFCu) >> ((a & 3u) * 8u)) & 255u; } \
+VG_FN uint vr_be16(uint pt, uint a) { return (vr_b(pt, a) << 8u) | vr_b(pt, a + 1u); } \
+VG_FN uint vr_be32(uint pt, uint a) { \
+    uint w = VR_RAW(pt, a & 0xFFFFFFFCu); \
+    if ((a & 3u) != 0u) w = vr_b(pt, a) | (vr_b(pt, a + 1u) << 8u) | (vr_b(pt, a + 2u) << 16u) | (vr_b(pt, a + 3u) << 24u); \
+    return (w >> 24u) | ((w >> 8u) & 0xFF00u) | ((w << 8u) & 0xFF0000u) | (w << 24u); \
+} \
+VG_FN float vr_fetch(uint pt, uint base, uint stride, uint fmt, uint lim, float dflt, uint e, uint c) { \
+    uint t = fmt & 15u; \
+    uint n = (fmt >> 4u) & 15u; \
+    uint a = base + e * stride; \
+    if (t == 0u) return dflt; \
+    if (a > lim) a = lim; \
+    if (t == 6u) { \
+        uint w = vr_be32(pt, a); \
+        if (c == 0u) return VG_LUT(65792u + (w & 0x7FFu)); \
+        if (c == 1u) return VG_LUT(65792u + ((w >> 11u) & 0x7FFu)); \
+        if (c == 2u) return VG_LUT(67840u + (w >> 22u)); \
+        return 1.0f; \
+    } \
+    if (c >= n) return c == 3u ? 1.0f : 0.0f; \
+    if (t == 2u) return asfloat(vr_be32(pt, a + c * 4u)); \
+    if (t == 3u) { \
+        uint h = vr_be16(pt, a + c * 2u); \
+        uint x = h & 0x7C00u; \
+        uint mag = ((h & 0x7FFFu) << 13u) + (x == 0x7C00u ? (224u << 23u) : (112u << 23u)); \
+        return asfloat(((h & 0x8000u) << 16u) | (x != 0u ? mag : 0u)); \
+    } \
+    if (t == 4u) return VG_LUT(vr_b(pt, a + c)); \
+    if (t == 7u) return (float)vr_b(pt, a + c); \
+    if (t == 1u) return VG_LUT(256u + vr_be16(pt, a + c * 2u)); \
+    if (t == 5u) return (float)(asint(vr_be16(pt, a + c * 2u) << 16u) >> 16); \
+    return 0.0f; \
+} )
+
+/* What the vertex shader declares (HLSL) for this mode: t20 the draw table, t22 the pool, t21 the decode table. */
+#define RSX_VR_HLSL_HEAD \
+    "ByteAddressBuffer vg_raw : register(t20);\n" \
+    "ByteAddressBuffer vg_lut : register(t21);\n" \
+    "ByteAddressBuffer vr_pool : register(t22);\n" \
+    "#define VG_FN\n" \
+    "#define VR_RAW(pt, a) vr_pool.Load((vg_raw.Load((pt) + ((a) >> 12u) * 4u) << 12u) | ((a) & 4095u))\n" \
+    "#define VG_LUT(i) asfloat(vg_lut.Load((i) * 4u))\n"
+#define RSX_VR_HLSL_TAIL \
+    "float4 vg_attr(uint i, uint e) {\n" \
+    "    uint r = i * 48u;\n" \
+    "    uint b = vg_raw.Load(r); uint s = vg_raw.Load(r + 4u); uint f = vg_raw.Load(r + 8u); uint l = vg_raw.Load(r + 12u);\n" \
+    "    uint p = vg_raw.Load(r + 16u);\n" \
+    "    return float4(vr_fetch(p, b, s, f, l, asfloat(vg_raw.Load(r + 32u)), e, 0u),\n" \
+    "                  vr_fetch(p, b, s, f, l, asfloat(vg_raw.Load(r + 36u)), e, 1u),\n" \
+    "                  vr_fetch(p, b, s, f, l, asfloat(vg_raw.Load(r + 40u)), e, 2u),\n" \
+    "                  vr_fetch(p, b, s, f, l, asfloat(vg_raw.Load(r + 44u)), e, 3u));\n" \
+    "}\n"
+
+/* One row of the draw table. */
+typedef struct { uint32_t base, stride, fmt, lim, pt, pad[3]; float dflt[4]; } vr_row;
+
+/* Build the draw table from 2076's plan of the same draw (rows relative to its block, spans with host addresses) and
+ * the block lists of its spans (lists[k] = vr_map_span's out for span k, npages[k] its count). dst holds
+ * VR_TABLE_BYTES + 4 * (sum of npages). Returns the bytes written. Row base / lim become span-relative addresses
+ * (from the span's first page), the same element addresses 2076 reads, so the decode is unchanged. */
+#ifdef PS3RECOMP_RSX_VTX_GPU_H
+static inline uint32_t vr_write_table(const rsx_vg_draw* d, const uint32_t* const* lists, const uint32_t* npages,
+                                      uint8_t* dst)
+{
+    uint32_t pt[RSX_DSP_NUM_VERTEX_ATTR], off = VR_TABLE_BYTES;
+    for (uint32_t k = 0; k < d->n_span; k++) {
+        pt[k] = off;
+        memcpy(dst + off, lists[k], 4u * npages[k]);
+        off += 4u * npages[k];
+    }
+    for (uint32_t a = 0; a < 16u; a++) {
+        const rsx_vg_attr* t = &d->table[a];
+        vr_row r; memset(&r, 0, sizeof r);
+        memcpy(r.dflt, t->dflt, sizeof r.dflt);
+        r.fmt = t->fmt;
+        if (t->fmt & 15u) {
+            uint32_t k = 0;
+            while (k + 1u < d->n_span && !(t->lim >= d->span[k].dst && t->lim < d->span[k].dst + d->span[k].bytes)) k++;
+            const uint32_t shift = (uint32_t)((uintptr_t)d->span[k].src & (VR_PAGE - 1u)) - d->span[k].dst;
+            r.base = t->base + shift; r.lim = t->lim + shift; r.stride = t->stride; r.pt = pt[k];
+        }
+        memcpy(dst + a * VR_ROW_BYTES, &r, sizeof r);
+    }
+    return off;
+}
+#endif
